| The plans (#3265, #3267): `forge/plan` on the host, and the hierarchy on every `ForgeItem` (`parent`, `level`, `feature`, `progress`) with a `feature` filter on the lists. Priority and on hold (#5688, #5747): `priority` and `onHold` on every `ForgeItem`, from the forge's own field where it has one, and then the labels are not read for it: Linear's and Jira's priority, GitHub's **Priority** issue field when the repo has it (Urgent and High → high; else the labels), Bitbucket's priority (blocker and critical → high, major → none, minor and trivial → low) and its state **on hold**, and Azure DevOps' **Priority** (1 → high, 2 → none, 3 and 4 → low); elsewhere the labels `priority:high`, `priority:medium` and `priority:low`, and `on hold` (any case; `on-hold` too), and on Jira a status named On hold too. Tested with fakes (`Go/internal/agentsd/forgepriority_test.go`, the forge packages' own); GitHub's issue fields read on github.com, and asked again without them where GitHub refuses them (GitHub Enterprise Server). GitHub: an epic's sub-issues and each one's `blockedBy`, in one GraphQL query; `parent` and `subIssuesSummary` in every list. GitLab: the work items' hierarchy and "blocked by" links (GitLab Premium; on Free every child is in step 1) by GraphQL, and the children by one REST list per project; `parent` and progress on an issue's own read and in a plan; `forge/next` reads the parents of a list's issues and epics by GraphQL, one query for each project and 100 issues (#7343), so an epic on hold or with an open blocker counts for the issues under it. Forgejo: `forge/next` gives an issue no parent, because an epic's children are the issues it depends on, and those are its blockers too (#7343). Linear: an issue's children and the "blocks" relations on them, in one GraphQL query; progress on an issue's own read and in a plan. Steps are worked out on the host; the lead is the session labelled with the epic and `lead`, from lineage. | none yet (Mac and web draw it in #3268) | tested on a real account (GitHub, GitLab) | — | 2026-11-04 (#3412): GitHub's plan of a new epic on alexec/agents-walk with two sub-issues, one blocked by the other and then not; GitLab's of a new issue with a task under it on agentstest-group/agents-walk (GitLab Free: issue to task only); 2026-11-02, GitHub's plan, search and item queries run on alexec/Agents#3265 by hand; `Go/internal/githubmcp/forgeplan_test.go`, `Go/internal/gitlabmcp/forgeplan_test.go`, `Go/internal/linearmcp/forgeplan_test.go` and `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeplan_test.go` (steps, a loop, blockers outside the plan, the lead, the feature filter) | `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeplan.go`, `Go/internal/githubmcp/forge.go`, `Go/internal/gitlabmcp/forge.go`, `Go/internal/linearmcp/forge.go` | Linear's query not yet run against its API (#3412: Alex signs in to Linear first); GitLab's blocked-by links not run (GitLab Premium; agentstest is on Free); a Linear or GitLab list says no progress (it would cost a page of children for each issue); GitLab's parents in `forge/next` (#7343) tested with fakes only (`Go/internal/agentsd/forgenext_test.go`), not on a real account |
